  {
   "attachments": {},
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "c7474bad-7b74-45cc-a6cc-49dc9cc37406",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "Recalling that the linearized carbonate system looks like:\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\\delta F_{\\mathrm{CO_2}} \\approx -\\frac{k}{\\beta}\\left(\\delta[\\mathrm{DIC}] - \\eta\\,\\delta[\\mathrm{ALK}]\\right)\n",
    "$$\n",
    "Where `k` is the gas transfer velocity, and `eta` and `beta` are the sensitivities here. Interpretation of the values aren't straightforward. Lower `beta` has the *potential* to increase gas exchange, but this is still first-order controlled by winds. "
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "df219c8c-2276-43cd-92ee-e818721355da",
   "metadata": {},
